      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Heat is a form of energy that flows from a body at a higher temperature to a body at a lower temperature.",
        "Temperature measures the degree of hotness or coldness of a body using scales like Celsius, Fahrenheit, and Kelvin.",
        "Heat transfer occurs via three primary mechanisms: Conduction, Convection, and Radiation.",
        "Most substances expand upon heating, with water exhibiting anomalous expansion between 0 °C and 4 °C."
      ],
      "id": "xqc2e1e"
    },
